arml-2025-power-01b.body:
The $\{2,3\}$-integers up to $15$ are $1,2,3,4,6,8,9,12$. Searching by length (no single part equals $15$, which is not a $\{2,3\}$-integer):
- length $2$: $(3,12)$, $(6,9)$;
- length $3$: $(1,2,12)$, $(1,6,8)$, $(2,4,9)$, $(3,4,8)$;
- length $4$: $(1,2,3,9)$, $(1,2,4,8)$, $(2,3,4,6)$;
- length $5$ would need five distinct parts summing to $15$, the least possible sum being $1+2+3+4+6=16>15$. None.

So there are exactly nine.
